    <briefdescription>
<para>Abstract base class for all loss functions. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1Criterion" kindref="compound">Criterion</ref> class defines the interface for computing loss values during neural network training. Specific loss functions such as cross-entropy or mean squared error are intended to derive from this class and implement the calculateLoss method with the appropriate loss computation. The resulting loss tensor participates in the computational graph, allowing gradients to be propagated back through the loss function during backpropagation.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1TensorView" kindref="compound">TensorView</ref> for the tensor class used to represent inputs, targets and loss values. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
